[size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]WHAT IT DOES[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Open any quickhack[/b] from its Quickhacks view, or by clicking one in REDcode, and see every tier in plain words: name, icon, RAM, upload time, cooldown, duration, damage and the effects it applies, with what scales them in the game.
[*][b]Change it:[/b] texts, icons, costs and numbers, for one tier or every tier at once. Your numbers are kept as numbers, not differences, so they survive game patches.
[*][b]Make new ones:[/b] Clone and Modify a game quickhack into a new one of your own, beside it, with its own records and cooldown. It is sold and crafted the way the game's tier it started from is.
[*][b]Add effects:[/b] borrow another quickhack's effect (Contagion's poison for Overheat), add any of the game's status effects on the target or on V, or build a damage over time, a stat change or a chance to apply.
[*][b]Icons of your own:[/b] upload pictures, or have OpenAI's GPT Image draw them from your words, with your own OpenAI key.
[*][b]Scripts:[/b] a scan check that decides per person whether the quickhack is usable, and a function when it lands, in JavaScript, run in the game by REDnode.
[*][b]Feature lines:[/b] bullets of your own in the item's tooltip, for what your scripts and effects do.
[*][b]Try Live:[/b] send a change into the running game through REDnode, with no packing, and put a new quickhack in V's backpack. Stop puts the game back.
[*][b]The Desk and the EDGE Library:[/b] work on quickhacks outside a project, and keep your best ones in the Library every EDGE tool shares, to take into any mod.
[*][b]Assistants:[/b] an MCP server lets Claude Code, or REDagent inside the game, make and change quickhacks with you. They ask you before every change.
[*][b]A mod you can read:[/b] EDGEhack writes TweakXL and ArchiveXL files into your REDcode project, and REDcode packs and installs it.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]WHAT YOU NEED[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Windows, Cyberpunk 2077 game 2.5, and [url=https://code.visualstudio.com/]VS Code[/url] 1.90 or later.
[*][url=https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=edgemodders.redcode-cyberpunk]REDcode[/url] 0.10.8 or later, from the VS Code Marketplace: install it first. It reads the game through REDbridge and holds your project.
[*]For the mods you make: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4197]TweakXL[/url], [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/4198]ArchiveXL[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/1511]redscript[/url].
[*]Optional: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/cyberpunk2077/mods/35419]REDnode[/url] 0.61.1 or later for scripts, 0.62.0 for Try Live; an OpenAI key for drawn icons.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#fcee0a]INSTALL[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]From this download: unzip it, then in VS Code open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X), click ... at its top, choose Install from VSIX..., and pick the .vsix inside.
[*]Or from [url=https://open-vsx.org/extension/edgemodders/edgehack]Open VSX[/url], in VSCodium, Cursor and other editors that use it. The VS Code Marketplace listing is on its way.
[*]Open EDGEhack's icon in the activity bar, and open your WolvenKit project in REDcode.
[/list]

